From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:35:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SP: aim assist for a gamepad, as DOOM 3 BFG's (cg_aimAssist)

DOOM 3 BFG Edition helps a gamepad aim; this is the same, by its rules
and numbers (AimAssist.cpp), for the single player:

- The target: the best enemy in front within 3000 units that can be seen
  (0.8 for looking at it, 0.2 for being near), its chest or else its head.
  An enemy is a living character of another team than the player's that
  is not neutral: civilians and allies never pull the aim.
- Friction: while the line of aim passes near it (96 units, 192 at 768),
  turning with the gamepad's stick slows down, to 0.4 on the target.
- Adhesion: while the player moves, the view turns towards a target near
  the line of aim (96 units): a quarter of what is left and 0.6 degrees
  at most a 60 Hz frame, compounded for other frame times.

The cgame (cg_aimassist.c) works it out each frame and hands it to the
client by a new trap, CG_SETAIMASSIST (after iortcw's CG_ALLOC); the
client slows the stick's turning (not the mouse's) and adds the turn to
the next command. cg_aimAssist 0 (the default) turns it off.
